Text of a letter from Police Commissioner Klutz dated August 13:

Dear Inspector,

     I heard today that the jury in the Robner case has voted to acquit Mr.
Baxter of both murders at the Robner house.
The jury believed the more probable story: that Ms. Dunbar committed the first
murder and then committed suicide when her guilt became clear to you. I don't
really believe this any more than you do, but the evidence is vague, you must
agree. Thanks again for handling the case.



The case has ended. Would you like to start your investigation over from
scratch? (Y/N) >